A||||9||1986 Fiero||Can i get any more horsepower out of a 2.5 4cyl?||||1||
Z||000000||1986 Fiero||03-16-2001||11:00 AM||||Like i just posted i just bought a 1986 fiero 2.5 4cyl.Do they sell chips for 4 cyl? Or can i get anymore power out of this little car?<BR>              Thanks||||reg||1
Z||000001||LuckyTheyWereEverMade||03-16-2001||11:59 AM||||There are no aftermarket chips for the Iron Duke.  But, there's lots of stuff you can do to get more power.<P>Replace the pellet cat with a modern high flow catalytic converter<P>Port the cylinder head and do a 3 angle valve job<P>change camshafts to a mild performance cam<P>Holley TBI (40% more airflow)<P>and more . . .<P>Just do a Forum search on "Iron Duke" in Technical Discussions and you should find a wealth of info!<P>The mods work well, my automatic 4 cylinder is doing 0 to 60 in about 9 seconds now.  It was about 11 when I started.  I'll post Dyno numbers this weekend . . .stay tuned!<BR>||||reg||1
Z||000002||Cheever2||03-16-2001||12:44 PM|||| <BLOCKQUOTE><font size="1" face="Verdana, Arial, Helvetica">quote:</font><HR>I'll post Dyno numbers this weekend . . .<HR></BLOCKQUOTE>I'll be watching... I'm very interested.  Maybe a rebuild will be a summer project with my boys (good excuse to put a/c in the garage), and I'll want to be prepared.  Their school ends around May 31.<P>||||reg||6
Z||000003||wjluciano||03-16-2001||03:37 PM||||check into a ignition mallory makes a great laser distributer along with a better ignition. also dynojet should have a power commander so you can remap your own fuel injection according to manifold presure, imting and throttle position. also look for the spark plug wires with capasiters they come in 8mm and 8.8 accell may make them also they provide pure power to your plugs without causing harm to your pistons. and change thaqt cat. thats about the only bolt on horse power i can think of||||reg||1
Z||000004||1FST2M6||03-16-2001||04:19 PM||||WOOO WHO!!! somone ponying up some real 4cyl numbers!  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/smile.gif"> it'll be pretty sad if you pull better numbers than some of us V6 owners!  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/smile.gif">||||reg||1
Z||000005||Mr.Frosty||03-16-2001||04:41 PM||||One thing I'll say for the Duke is Pontiac<BR>had a sh*t load of high performance parts made for it in it's day(Super duty)If you look in the road&track book that FOCOA used to sell,and look at the Indy pace\race program in it.You'll see that it made 275HP<BR>with the crank,pistons,cam,intake,head,etc,etc.With tuning they got 300HP.It did 0-60 in 4.0 sec.flat.It was also technically a 2.7 ltr.<BR>motor.If you can find those GM parts,that would "Kick Arse", but I heard they're hard to find.I had a Duke for my first fiero 7 years ago and did the holly intake,TBI thing but I fell in love with that first Formula.The only drawback to the Hi-po duke was engine longevity.But tooling around town and not racing all the time it would be worth it.  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/eek.gif"><P>------------------<BR>88 Formula T-top <BR>85 GT Turbo||||reg||10
